# Line endings are NOT converted. This is a correctness requirement, not a
# style preference.
#
# A data artifact's rollup hash is a SHA-256 over its bytes. If git rewrote
# LF <-> CRLF on checkout, the same artifact would hash differently on the
# Windows laptop and on the Linux cluster, and guard 3 would abort every cluster
# run with a hash mismatch that had nothing to do with the data.
* -text

# Shell scripts are the one exception: they must be LF everywhere or the
# cluster's interpreter line fails with "bad interpreter". They are never hashed
# as data artifacts, so normalising them is safe.
*.sh text eol=lf
